{"step_index":208,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-06T08:24:55Z","content":"The admin can add multiple photos through the **Product Photography Gallery Manager** in the Admin Portal.\n\n---\n\n### How the Admin Adds Multiple Photos\n\n1. **Navigate to the Admin Portal**:\n   - Go to `http://localhost:5173/admin`\n   - Sign in as Admin (`admin@cakenflowers.com` / `AdminPassword123!` or use the one-click **\"Demo Admin\"** button).\n   - Click the **\"Catalog & Stock\"** tab.\n\n2. **Add Photos (Two Convenient Ways)**:\n   - **Method A — Direct File Upload from Computer**:\n     - Click **\"Upload Photos from Device\"**.\n     - In the file picker, select multiple images at once (using `Ctrl+Click` or `Shift+Click`).\n     - The files are automatically processed via `POST /api/uploads/multiple` and saved directly to the backend `/uploads` directory.\n   - **Method B — Paste External Hosted URLs**:\n     - Paste image URLs from Unsplash, Cloudinary, AWS S3, or any CDN into the text box and click **\"+ Add URL\"**.\n\n3. **Manage the Photo Gallery & Set the Cover Photo**:\n   - As photos are added, interactive thumbnail cards appear in a gallery grid below.\n   - **Cover Photo**: The first photo is automatically marked with the `★ Cover` badge and serves as the primary catalog card thumbnail.\n   - **Reorder Cover**: Hover over any other photo and click **\"Make Cover\"** to promote it to the primary slot.\n   - **Remove Photo**: Hover over any thumbnail and click the 🗑️ trash button to delete it from the gallery.\n\n4. **Publish Product**:\n   - Fill in the product name, category, price, and description, then click **\"Publish Product\"**.\n   - The database stores the images as a JSON array (`images: [\"/uploads/photo1.jpg\", \"/uploads/photo2.jpg\", ...]`).\n   - When customers view the product on the storefront, the **Product Detail Page** will automatically display the multi-image gallery with thumbnail switcher previews."}
